3. Artificial intelligence systems

"AI System" means any artificial intelligence or machine learning system,
application, model, agent, assistant, bot or automated tool, together with
anyone who operates or deploys it.

Unless the Owner has explicitly authorised it, no AI System may:

  (a) modify, add to, delete, rewrite, refactor, move or otherwise change any
      part of the Software;
  (b) commit, push, merge or open pull requests against any repository that
      holds the Software, or take any other action on it;
  (c) copy, reproduce or distribute the Software, or create derivative works
      from it; or
  (d) use the Software to train, fine-tune, evaluate or build any AI model or
      dataset, or to support retrieval for one.

Authorisation is explicit only when the Owner personally grants it to a
specific AI System for specific work, for example by personally starting
and instructing that AI System, in a session the Owner controls, to work on
the Software. It does not carry over to any other AI System, session or
task. Anything an AI System does without such authorisation is unlicensed
and infringes the Owner's rights.

